+# R35 UI quiet change — host-only, 2026-11-20
+
+Delivered `ports/hakios-lithium/patches/0025-lithium-ui-performance.patch`.
+It patches the existing **xnu/hakios.patch** kern_exec diff, after R34/0024.
+The enclosing added-line count changes from 57 to 71; all subsequent kern_exec
+new-side hunk coordinates advance by 14. Normal prepare/rebuild can reproduce
+the change. `actual-kern-exec.patch` is the matching delta against the actual
+R34 generated `xnu-src/xnu-8796.121.2/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c`, for main's
+incremental application after prepare, without re-extraction.
+
+The latest user observation is that applications are usable, touch position,
+swipe and long press are normal, while SpringBoard home/app switcher remains
+severely laggy. This is user feedback, not a new host or device measurement.
+The change targets a plausible synchronous logging amplifier; its performance
+benefit is unmeasured.
+
+## Minimal production change
+
+- Adds `static TUNABLE(uint32_t, exec_applog_ui_quiet, "applog_ui_quiet", 0)`.
+- Only value **1** enables the gate. Absent/0 preserves prior behavior.
+- In `exec_applog_oslog`, before `exec_applog >= 2`, length and bytes must
+  match exactly `backboardd` or `SpringBoard` before returning false.
+  Prefixes, suffixes and case variants retain their prior behavior.
+- Prevents this function from requesting the extra `OS_ACTIVITY_DT_MODE=YES`
+  entry. Existing envp entries are retained. `exec_extract_strings` and
+  `exec_applog_path` are unchanged. fd1/fd2 routing, explicit stderr writes,
+  other processes and ordinary logging remain as before.
+- No helper, touch redesign, UI code or preference changes were made.
+
+## Launchd environment provenance
+
+Actual patched sources were read, not upstream-only approximations:
+
+1. `userland/root/etc/rc` contains `exec /sbin/launchd.darwin`.
+2. Actual `userland/src/init.c:1424-1429` constructs a fresh envp with
+   `PATH=/var/jb/usr/bin:/var/jb/bin:/var/jb/usr/sbin:/var/jb/sbin:/bin:/sbin:/usr/bin:/usr/sbin`,
+   `HOME=/var/mobile`, `TERM=dumb`. The launchd exec at 1498-1501 uses that
+   envp, not parent `environ`; flash-root selects `/sbin/launchd`.
+3. The frozen R34 UFS `boot-args.txt` has
+   `applog=1 applog_name=backboardd,SpringBoard`. This does not select
+   launchd or xpcproxy for the kernel's forced DT_MODE entry.
+4. Read-only plist decoding confirms backboardd has no EnvironmentVariables
+   dictionary; SpringBoard has only `CA_ASSERT_MAIN_THREAD_TRANSACTIONS=1`.
+   Both set `StandardErrorPath=/dev/console`; neither supplies DT_MODE.
+5. `scripts/build-hakios-ios16-userspace.py:53-56` sets build `OSLOG=''`
+   for the existing R9 diagnostic branch, and 130-134 verifies absence of
+   DT_MODE in those jobs. Preserve that generated-plist condition during
+   regeneration: upstream `userland/build.sh:468` otherwise defaults OSLOG
+   to backboardd; `mkjobs.py:275,302` can add DT_MODE independently.
+
+This verifies the inspected source/configuration path, not the live launchd
+domain environment. A caller, job, launchd-domain setting, or kernel injection
+into launchd/xpcproxy under a different `applog>=2`/name configuration can
+still provide/inherit DT_MODE. **R35 does not delete or override it.**
+In particular, testing the gate at applog=2 proves the gate's return value,
+not that inherited os_log echo is globally disabled.
+Source and plist hashes are in `reference.json`.
+
+## Optional package profiles, for main
+
+| Candidate | Boot-argument addition to R34 | Effect/persistence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Quiet only | `applog_ui_quiet=1` | Gate is default-off and selected per boot; keeps existing applog/name arguments. Does not write preferences. |
+| Quiet plus existing UI lite | `applog_ui_quiet=1 ui_lite=1` | Separate optional candidate: existing SpringBoard hook writes both settings below. |
+| Explicit UI lite reversal | `ui_lite=0` | Writes both settings false; omission alone does not undo prior values. |
