+| CFPreferences key | Domain | Value for `ui_lite=1` |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `EnhancedBackgroundContrastEnabled` | `com.apple.Accessibility` | `kCFBooleanTrue` (Reduce Transparency) |
+| `ReduceMotionEnabled` | `com.apple.Accessibility` | `kCFBooleanTrue` (Reduce Motion) |
+
+Both use `kCFPreferencesCurrentUser` / `kCFPreferencesAnyHost`.
+It calls `CFPreferencesSynchronize` for that domain, then posts
+`com.apple.accessibility.cache.enhance.background.contrast` and
+`com.apple.accessibility.cache.reduce.motion`. The synchronization result is
+not checked by the existing code. ui_lite=0 writes false to both; no argument
+leaves them alone. Use the exact arguments above; this existing parser uses
+the first value character (`0` versus anything else).
+
+Persistence is a real setting change, not a temporary animation flag:
+with the R34 HFS Data mount (`var_hfs=ufs_darwin_data`), preferences are
